            <ArticleTitle>Surgical treatment of trigger fingers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The surgical treatment of 55 trigger fingers resulted in 87% patient satisfaction, without major complications. The mean incapacity was 1.4 weeks. Three recurrences were noted; four patients had a slight extension lag and three still experienced some local pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
